rapped error, but cobra's usage block is suppressed (good). The corresponding paths.WorktreeRoot at line 203 in the same function DOES set `SilenceUsage = true` AND prints a custom message — the inconsistency between the two prerequisite paths is the issue. Same gap exists in `runMultiAgentPath` at cmd.go:496-503.\n\n**Recommendation:** Set `cmd.SilenceUsage = true` for the WorktreeRoot and HEAD-resolution branches too. They're prerequisite failures — usage text is not useful here.\n\n---\n\n### 6. MEDIUM — `reviewContextCommitMessages` failure silently swallows the entire committed-checkpoint section\n**Location:** `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/review-fix-2/cmd/entire/cli/review_context.go:89-95`\n\n```go\nmessages, commitsTruncated, err := reviewContextCommitMessages(ctx, worktreeRoot, scopeBaseRef, reviewContextMaxCommitScans)\nif err != nil || len(messages) == 0 {\n    if err != nil {\n        logging.Debug(ctx, \"review checkpoint context: list commit messages\", slog.String(\"error\", err.Error()))\n    }\n    return \"\"\n}\n```\n\nThis is mostly fine — the \"best-effort context\" contract is real and well-documented. BUT the predicate `err != nil || len(messages) == 0` conflates two very different conditions: \"git log subprocess died\" (an error worth investigating) and \"the branch genuinely has no commits ahead of base\" (expected, common, totally benign). Both get a return of `\"\"` with no operator trace in the empty-result case. That's correct behaviour per design, but the operator who runs `entire review --base feat/parent` and sees no checkpoint context has no way to tell which case fired.\n\n**Recommendation:** Add a single debug line in the empty-list case too:\n\n```go\nif err != nil {\n    logging.Debug(ctx, \"review checkpoint context: list commit messages\", slog.String(\"error\", err.Error()))\n    return \"\"\n}\nif len(messages) == 0 {\n    logging.Debug(ctx, \"review checkpoint context: no commits in s